{"path":"neuron_growth_openai-gpt-5.6-terra_01.html","edit_description":"Create this new single-file HTML application. It must contain one centered 800x800 canvas on a #05070f page, vanilla HTML/CSS/JS, and a single CDN script for dat.gui (no other dependencies/assets). Build a compact neon neural-network growth simulation matching all requested behavior: exact defaults palette #05070f, #101a3a, #00e5ff, #d6ff00, #ff2bd6, #fff36a, #ffd400 and optional rgba(0,229,255,0.08); canvas shadowBlur glow, canvas-only scanlines/noise and vignette. Include visible small title/help overlay if desired but keep canvas only as drawing surface.

Use clearly commented sections: setup, GUI setup, neuron growth, synapse detection, pulse animation, rendering. Implement lightweight arrays: branches (each stores start/end/control, growth progress, depth, thickness, accent, finished), tips/queued growth jobs, synapses (two branches or endpoint positions), pulses. Seed a randomized count configured 3–6, near center. Add initial jobs and process a capped number of growing branches each animation frame; each branch becomes visible step-by-step according to growthSpeed, draws partial quadratic curve, then queues 1–3 children subject to maxDepth, splitChance, maxLength, and global branch cap. Smooth random direction/curvature, varied thickness and occasional side branches. Detect nearby tips/endpoints on completed branches using a bounded nested loop and create uniquely keyed synapses when within threshold, requiring distinct branches; clear/rebuild synapses after each growth completion or periodically. Synapses must softly pulse. Periodically spawn spark pulses across synapses based on pulseFrequency, interpolate their positions with pulseSpeed and remove after progress >1. Keep it alive after growth ends through continuing pulse spawn/animation.

Create dat.GUI instance and folders exactly named Growth, Synapses, Pulses, Visuals. Controls: neuronCount (integer 3–6), growthSpeed, maxDepth, splitChance, curvature, maxBranchLength in Growth; synapseDistance and synapseGlow in Synapses; pulseSpeed, pulseFrequency, pulseBrightness in Pulses; backgroundColor, branchColor, accentBranchColor, synapseColor, pulseColor in Visuals. Provide actions named regenerateNetwork, clearCanvas, pauseResume with readable labels via .name('regenerate network'), .name('clear canvas'), .name('pause/resume animation'). Regenerate applies configuration and starts anew; clear canvas empties network and persists a blank scene; pause resume toggles a flag. Changes that affect generation should regenerate only when finished editing; visual colors update immediately. Ensure the GUI CSS is styled with yellow #ffd400 accent and does not add any external assets. Avoid all references to games, movies, brands, or copyrighted visual styles in code/comments other than the necessary dat.gui library identifier. Use requestAnimationFrame, avoid expensive systems/pathfinding, remain robust if dat.GUI namespace fails by displaying a small text notice rather than crashing."}

